course: dictionary
lesson: 14852
title: Formal words for speed
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Rapidity is a formal word for speed. It means how fast something happens. «The rapidity of the reaction surprised the scientists.» The reaction happened quickly, so rapidity must mean speed.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «The runner crossed the line with great rapidity.» The words «with great» tell you it was a lot, and a runner crossing a line fast fits with speed. Try the swap: «with great speed» still makes sense, so you have found the meaning.
explain: Notice the ending. Rapid means quick, and rapidity is the noun form, the name of the quality. You will often see rapidity in serious writing and science, and in stories it can sound grand, as if the author wants you to notice the speed.
fact: Rapidity means great speed, or how fast something happens.
fact: «With great rapidity» means very fast.
fact: Rapidity is a formal word, so you will meet it more in science and serious writing than in everyday talk.
fact: Rapidity is uncountable: you say «great rapidity», not «a rapidity» or «three rapidities».
fact: Simpler words for rapidity are speed, pace and quickness.
exercise: «The cheetah ran with great rapidity across the grass.» What does rapidity mean here? | Great size | *Great speed | Great patience | Great silence
exercise: «The rapidity of the reaction amazed the class.» Find and copy the one word that is the noun for speed. | amazed | the | reaction | *rapidity
exercise: Mia says rapidity means how slow something is. What does rapidity really mean? | How heavy something is | How slow something is | How loud something is | *How fast something happens
test: Which plain word means nearly the same as rapidity? | *Speed | Colour | Height | Silence
test: «They were amazed by the rapidity with which the fire spread.» What does rapidity show here? | How hot the fire was | How big the fire was | The colour of the flames | *How fast the fire spread
exam: Which word is a noun meaning speed? | rapidly | rapture | rapid | *rapidity
